    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d554">

                <pb facs="0450" n="438" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg438"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">882.515/76: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Chargé in Liberia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Hibbard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-09-26T14:00:00-04:00">September 26,
                            1942—2 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>236. Your 291, September 9, 6 p.m., your 287, September 3, 5 p.m., and your
                    784–A, September 3.<anchor n="76" xml:id="d554-f1"/> You may advise the Liberian
                    Government that in view of their confirmation of the agreement for the
                    acquisition of British current coin in Liberia as contained in the Department’s
                    telegram 187, August 3, 8 p.m., the Treasury Department considers such agreement
                    to have been approved by the Liberian Government and to be in full force and
                    effect.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d554-f1" n="76" xml:id="d554-f1-content">
                <p>Despatch No. 784–A not printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
